@node Development Shells
@chapter Generating Files for Development Shells
@cindex development shells
@vindex perSystem.devshells
@vindex devShells.@var{system}.@var{name}

  The @code{devshell} module extends upstream devshell with generated
project files.  A shell's packages and settings use the usual devshell
options.  File entries add store files, startup links, and optional
hooks alongside those settings.

  Declare shells under @code{perSystem.devshells}, with a lowercase
@samp{s}.  It is an attribute set of submodules and defaults to @code{@{
@}}.  Each entry produces a flake output under
@code{devShells.@var{system}.@var{name}}, with a capital @samp{S}. The
system is selected by the flake-parts @code{systems} list. @xref{Getting
Started}, for the required inputs and imports.

@menu
* Defining a Shell::    Select packages and name the environment.
* Generated Files::    Turn Nix data into project configuration.
* Startup Actions::    Order links and run hooks.
* File Options::       Reference for generated file entries.
@end menu

@node Defining a Shell
@section Defining a Shell Environment

  A named shell entry is an upstream devshell module extended with a
@code{files} option.  Upstream options such as @code{commands},
@code{env}, @code{devshell.packages}, and @code{devshell.startup} remain
available. This module defines a shell containing Git and ripgrep:

@example
@{
  perSystem =
    @{
      pkgs,
      ...
    @}:
    @{
      devshells = @{
        default = @{
          devshell = @{
            name = "example";

            packages = with pkgs; [
              git
              ripgrep
            ];
          @};
        @};
      @};
    @};
@}
@end example

@noindent
For each configured platform, infix assigns
@code{perSystem.devshells.default.devshell.shell} to
@code{devShells.@var{system}.default}.  The same mapping applies to
other entry names.  Generated files are optional; an ordinary devshell
entry needs no @code{files} declarations.

@node Generated Files
@section Generating and Linking Project Files
@cindex generated files
@cindex store files
@cindex symbolic links
@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{name}.files

  The @code{files} attribute set maps entry names to generated files. It
defaults to @code{@{ @}}.  Each entry needs @code{data}, a
@code{generator}, and a destination @code{path}.  The generator receives
the data and returns a store file.  Entering the shell links that file
under the project root, as identified by @env{PRJ_ROOT}.

  The following module creates a JSON configuration.  Its entry name,
@samp{settings}, identifies the startup action; @code{path} selects the
actual destination file.

@example
@{
  perSystem =
    @{
      pkgs,
      ...
    @}:
    let
      json = pkgs.formats.json @{ @};
    in
    @{
      devshells = @{
        default = @{
          files = @{
            settings = @{
              data = @{
                formatter = "treefmt";

                language = "nix";
              @};

              generator = json.generate "settings.json";

              path = ".config/example/settings.json";
            @};
          @};
        @};
      @};
    @};
@}
@end example

@noindent
The name supplied to @code{json.generate} names the generated store
file.  It does not determine the link's destination.  Binding the name
leaves a function of one argument, the entry's @code{data}.

  Shell startup creates the destination's parent directories and runs
@command{ln} with @option{-sfnT} on the exact destination path.  This
can replace an existing file or symbolic link.  A directory at that path
is not treated as a destination directory for the link.  The generated
contents live in the Nix store; edit the Nix data to change them.

  Linking happens when the shell starts.  Producing the shell derivation
alone does not create files in the working directory.  Removing a file
entry does not remove a link left by an earlier shell session.

@node Startup Actions
@section Ordering Links and Running Hooks
@cindex startup ordering
@cindex file hooks

  Each file entry creates an upstream devshell startup entry with the
same name.  The @code{deps} list names startup entries that must run
first.  Dependencies may name other generated files or other upstream
startup entries; their names are not destination paths.

  A file's @code{hook} runs after its link has been created.  Use it for
an action that needs the generated file.  Packages listed in the file
entry's @code{packages} are added to @code{devshell.packages}, so tools
needed by hooks are available in the shell.

  This module links a routing file, validates it with @command{jq}, and
then links a second file whose startup entry depends on the first:

@example
@{
  perSystem =
    @{
      pkgs,
      ...
    @}:
    let
      json = pkgs.formats.json @{ @};
    in
    @{
      devshells = @{
        default = @{
          files = @{
            routing = @{
              data = @{
                target = "local";
              @};

              generator = json.generate "routing.json";

              hook = ''
                jq -e '.target == "local"' \
                  "$PRJ_ROOT/.config/example/routing.json" >/dev/null
              '';

              packages = with pkgs; [
                jq
              ];

              path = ".config/example/routing.json";
            @};

            settings = @{
              data = @{
                routing = "routing.json";
              @};

              deps = [
                "routing"
              ];

              generator = json.generate "settings.json";

              path = ".config/example/settings.json";
            @};
          @};
        @};
      @};
    @};
@}
@end example

@noindent
The @samp{settings} startup action depends on the entire @samp{routing}
action, including its hook.  Use distinct entry names for independent
startup actions.  Dependency resolution and startup error handling
follow the upstream devshell behavior.

@node File Options
@section Generated File Options

  The following fields belong to
@code{perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}}.  The file entry
name selects its startup entry; it does not supply defaults for the
fields below.

@table @code
@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.data
@item data
Required value of any Nix type.  It is passed unchanged to
@code{generator}, which determines the useful input types.  There is no
default.

@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.generator
@item generator
Required function taking @code{data} and returning a store file suitable
as a symbolic-link target.  There is no default.  Format generators from
@code{pkgs.formats} commonly take a file name before the data; bind that
name as shown in @ref{Generated Files}.

@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.path
@item path
Required nonempty string that does not start with @samp{/}.  The path is
appended to @env{PRJ_ROOT}.  There is no default.  Use a path within
your project; the option's type does not reject @samp{..} components.

@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.deps
@item deps
List of startup entry names; defaults to @code{[ ]}.  These actions must
precede the file's startup action.  @xref{Startup Actions}.

@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.hook
@item hook
Shell text appended after the linking commands; defaults to @code{""}.
It uses the module system's lines type.

@vindex perSystem.devshells.@var{shell}.files.@var{file}.packages
@item packages
List of packages added to the shell; defaults to @code{[ ]}.  Packages
from all file entries are combined with the shell's package definitions.
@end table

  The generated @code{file} value is internal.  Configure @code{data}
and @code{generator} instead of supplying that value directly.
